From: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mt7622: ramoops — add console/pmsg/ftrace capture

The MT7622 ramoops node reserves 64 KiB (0x42ff0000/0x10000) but declares only
record-size (the oops/panic dump zone). On a headless, no-UART board (Linksys
E8450) a *bus hang* — e.g. the WED attach fault — freezes the CPU without an
oops or panic, so the record zone captures nothing and the hang leaves no trace
across the power-cycle recovery.

Carve a console zone (continuously mirrors the kernel printk ring to persistent
RAM) plus pmsg/ftrace zones. Breadcrumb printk emitted immediately before a
hanging MMIO access then survives the freeze: after the manual power-cycle,
/sys/fs/pstore/console-ramoops-0 holds the last line printed before the hang,
pinpointing the offending access. Zones fit the existing 64 KiB reservation.

Signed-off-by: pat <pi3iman@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7622.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7622.dtsi
@@ -146,6 +146,9 @@
 			compatible = "ramoops";
 			reg = <0 0x42ff0000 0 0x10000>;
 			record-size = <0x1000>;
+			console-size = <0x8000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x1000>;
+			ftrace-size = <0x1000>;
 		};
 
 		/* 192 KiB reserved for ARM Trusted Firmware (BL31) */
